# What this repository does not track.
#
# No line begins with `!`: an exception means the previous line ignored something that had to
# be kept, which is an arbitration a `.gitignore` is not allowed to make.

# Everything a run writes and no reader opens: logs, the coverage database and its HTML
# report, scratch corpora built by the smoke and by the capture script.
var/

# The corpus a run collects. It is content, not litter — the dashboard and a model downstream
# read it — and it stays out of the repository for a different reason: the four sources are
# live, each keeps its own terms, and none of them is redistributed here. What IS tracked
# under data/ is the demonstration sample, which is synthetic and is an input.
data/raw/
data/interim/
data/processed/
data/db/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Tool caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Secrets. `.env.example` is tracked and is not matched by this line: it is `.env` exactly,
# so keeping the example needs no exception.
.env
.streamlit/secrets.toml
infra/.env
secrets.toml
*.pem
*.key

# Editors and operating systems
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
